  "caveats": [
    "Confounders: the 2023 tech layoffs, interest-rate rises, and shifts in who posts on Hacker News (posts per month fell from about 700 in 2019 to about 310) all hit tech skills at the same time.",
    "e_s has only 6 distinct values (one per category) and only 5 categories have an ok skill, so 40 skills carry 5 independent points. The cluster bootstrap and the category-level fit show this.",
    "The ai_ml skills (LLM / GenAI, RAG, Machine Learning, PyTorch) rose because they are AI skills. ai_ml also has the lowest e_s, so it can create a negative slope by itself. See excluding_ai_ml.",
    "e_s is built from AEI 2026-06 usage and is not time-cut: it is the same for every window.",
    "Categories are coarse: all languages share one e_s.",
    "k is cumulative over the window; the per-12-month version assumes an even build-up.",
    "The most recent window includes the partial month 2026-10.",
    "This is an association across skills, not proof that AI exposure caused the change."
  ]
